.PP
A literate\-programming task tracker that lives entirely in markdown.
The document \f[I]is\f[R] the task tree \[em] no database, no sidecar
files.
Status rides on the heading; everything else is recognized fields +
plain prose you read top to bottom.
.SH Format
.IP
.EX
## [IN\-PROGRESS] Wire keybinds
deadline:: 2026\-06\-10
schedule:: 2026\-06\-08
prio:: A
owner:: costa
tags:: ui, input

Prose under the heading is the literate description \[em] narrative,
code fences, sub\-lists.

\- 2026\-06\-08 14:30 split the parser into its own file
\- 2026\-06\-08 16:05 deadline pushed a day

## [DONE] OSC52 clipboard
completed:: 2026\-06\-08
Works over SSH, verified on alacritty + tmux.
.EE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Status\f[R] = a \f[CR][KEYWORD]\f[R] immediately after the
\f[CR]#\f[R]s.
A heading with no keyword is just a heading, not a task \[em] prose and
tasks coexist.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Fields\f[R] = \f[CR]key:: value\f[R] lines directly under the
heading (Dataview/Logseq style).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Notes\f[R] = see Notes below.
.PP
Statuses: \f[CR]TODO\f[R] · \f[CR]IN\-PROGRESS\f[R] · \f[CR]BLOCKED\f[R]
(open) and \f[CR]DONE\f[R] · \f[CR]CANCELLED\f[R] (closed).
