.PP
Dates are \f[CR]YYYY\-MM\-DD\f[R].
The highlighter colours recognized field keys and validates values: a
good date renders green, garbage red, and the priority is coloured by
level (A red, B amber, C blue).
Unrecognized field keys are left as plain text.
.SH Notes
Two tiers, both plain markdown:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Body prose\f[R] under the heading is the description \[em] the
literate part.
Write freely: paragraphs, code fences, sub\-lists.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]A dated log\f[R] at the end of the section.
\f[CR]:task_note <text>\f[R] appends
\f[CR]\- YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM <text>\f[R] just after the section\[cq]s
last non\-blank line.
Append\-only, chronological, greppable.
Closing a task additionally records the date in \f[CR]completed::\f[R].
